[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-API-002
VERSION: 1
TITLE: Error responses
STATEMENT: >>>
If the service rejects a calculation request, then the service **shall**
respond with HTTP status **400** and the JSON body
`{"error": <error code>, "message": <text>}`.
<<<
KIND: functional
STATUS: draft
PRIORITY: high
SAFETY: QM
RELEASE: 1.0.0
VERIFICATION: test
VERIF_LEVELS: integration, system
TAGS: api, http, json, validation
SOURCE: Stakeholder request, 2026-11-18
OWNER: msforenter090
CREATED: 2026-11-18T00:00:00Z
RATIONALE: >>>
One error format for every rejected request lets clients handle all errors
in one place. The error code is stable and meant for programs; the message
is meant for people and may change.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
- Error codes are defined in the glossary: `INVALID_NUMBER`,
  `DIVISION_BY_ZERO`, `MALFORMED_REQUEST`.
- The message is in English. Its exact text is not specified.
- Requests to unknown paths and with methods other than `POST` are not
  calculation requests; see REQ-API-001 AC-4 and AC-5.
<<<
